<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lincoln, England</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lincoln is a cathedral city in the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-witham">River Witham</a>. It began as the Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> fortress of Lindum, which became a colonia for veterans, later gave its name to the Anglian kingdom of Lindsey and was one of the Five Boroughs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danelaw">Danelaw</a>. Its Norman castle and cathedral, begun in 1072, dominate the hilltop, and two battles were fought there, in 1141 and 1217.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lincoln-england.jpg" alt="Lincoln, England" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tilman2007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1388680_Cathedral_Church_of_St_Mary,_West_Front_Lincoln_20240519_0252.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
